From 41ca97b4ccd0ce52a408c2270e04997b3f7e9bb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "djm@openbsd.org" <djm@openbsd.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:38:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] upstream: used cached hostname for `Match host` when
 UseDNS=yes;

avoids multiple lookups for same host and a different number of lookups when
the user exists vs not.

Anthropic ANT-2026-14BFHJ3R

OpenBSD-Commit-ID: 1a4b7cedcc2ccdb24eac9a1455f7c26b0437d442

[Hades: backported to 10.6p1 without the hunk that updates the
$OpenBSD$ ident comment on line 1 of monitor_wrap.c: in master that line
already carries a later revision, which goes back to ea2111b5622c
("upstream: clean up Kerberos ccache if KerberosAuthentication"), a commit that
10.6p1 does not have, so that hunk cannot apply. The code hunks are
the commit's, unchanged.]
---
 monitor_wrap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/monitor_wrap.c b/monitor_wrap.c
index c828fce..9870d84 100644
--- a/monitor_wrap.c
+++ b/monitor_wrap.c
@@ -1195,7 +1195,7 @@ server_get_connection_info(struct ssh *ssh, int populate, int use_dns)
 
 	if (ssh == NULL || !populate)
 		return &ci;
-	ci.host = use_dns ? ssh_remote_hostname(ssh) : ssh_remote_ipaddr(ssh);
+	ci.host = auth_get_canonical_hostname(ssh, use_dns);
 	ci.address = ssh_remote_ipaddr(ssh);
 	ci.laddress = ssh_local_ipaddr(ssh);
 	ci.lport = ssh_local_port(ssh);
